While I like the idea of enriching the long lived context so we can reuse the inference result from the query phase in the fetch phase, it seems very complicated to achieve it (maybe that is just me).

I tried another approach that consist of executing the rewrite conditionally, so most queries won't be affected by it:

```
    private void rewriteAndFetchShardRequestBeforeFetchPhase(
        IndexShard shard,
        ShardSearchRequest request,
        ActionListener<ShardSearchRequest> listener
    ) {
        if (request.source().explain() && request.source().rescores().stream().anyMatch(r -> r instanceof QueryRescorerBuilder == false)) {
            // Rewriting the shard request is useful only when explain is enabled and a learning to rank rescorer is used.
            rewriteAndFetchShardRequest(shard, request, listener);
            return;
        }

        listener.onResponse(request);
    }
```

Let me know what do you think of that approach.

